  "instance_name": "shocked_woman_stereotype",
  "label": "Shocked Woman Stereotype",
  "description": "A visual trope commonly used in media and memes to convey exaggerated shock, disbelief, or moral outrage. The image of a woman with wide eyes and hands on her head is often used to amplify the perceived 'shock value' of a claim, making it more likely to be shared and believed. In this meme, the stereotype is used to visually reinforce the false claim about the Bible, thereby making the misinformation more emotionally compelling and virulent.",
